# Costbook — Supabase.
#
# Copy to .env.local and fill in from your project's Settings → API.
# .env.local is gitignored; this file is the template and holds no secrets.
#
# Restart the dev server after editing — env is read at boot, not per request.

# Project URL, e.g. https://xxxxxxxxxxxx.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=

# The anon / publishable key. Safe in the browser by design — RLS is what
# protects the data, which is why the policies were written first.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# The service_role key, which bypasses row security entirely.
#
# This used to say the application never held it, and for a long time that was
# true: every write carried the caller's cookie and row security scoped it to
# their own book. The payment callback broke the rule, because it has to.
# Razorpay posts to /api/razorpay/webhook from its own servers with no cookie
# and no session — and under row security that request is nobody, so an update
# matches zero rows and SUCCEEDS. Nothing raises, nothing is written, and the
# money is already taken.
#
# It is read by exactly one module, lib/supabase/admin.ts, which is imported by
# exactly one other, lib/settle.ts, which is imported by that one route. No
# screen a person looks at reaches it. Nothing else in the product may.
#
# Treat it like the Razorpay secret, not like the anon key: no NEXT_PUBLIC_
# prefix, never in a bundle, never in a screenshot. Leaving it unset is safe —
# the callback refuses with a 503 and says so in the log — but every payment
# whose browser went away is then lost, which is the bug it exists to fix.
#
# Supabase dashboard: Project Settings -> API Keys -> service_role.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# ── Mail ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Until these are set, nothing is posted: a support reply is delivered inside
# Costbook and its copy waits in mail_outbox. Set them, restart, and press
# "Send waiting" on /admin/mail — the backlog goes out oldest first, each
# carrying the date it was written rather than the date it was finally sent.
RESEND_API_KEY=
MAIL_FROM=Costbook <hello@costbook.in>

# ── Payments ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Two variables, and the plans page reads them to decide what it can offer.
# Neither is public: the key id is handed to the browser by a server action
# when a checkout opens, so it never needs NEXT_PUBLIC_ and never sits in a
# bundle. The secret is read on the server only, to open an order and to
# verify the signature that comes back.
#
# Both come from the Razorpay dashboard, Settings -> API Keys. A key pair is
# either TEST or LIVE and the two are not interchangeable:
#
#   rzp_test_...   nothing is charged. Use this until a real card has been
#                  through the whole flow at least once.
#   rzp_live_...   real money. Only once the test pair has been proved.
#
# The secret is shown ONCE, when the pair is generated. If it was not saved,
# regenerate rather than guess — a wrong secret opens orders fine and then
# fails every signature check, which looks like customers being charged and
# refused.
#
# With these unset there is no payment path, and the plans page says so
# rather than pretending. Restart after editing: env is read at boot.
RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=
RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=

# The webhook secret, which is a THIRD secret and not either of the two above.
#
# Razorpay signs a webhook delivery over the whole request body with this,
# where it signs the browser's callback over order_id|payment_id with the API
# secret. They are not interchangeable and using one for the other's job fails
# every delivery.
#
# You choose this value yourself when registering the endpoint:
#
#   Dashboard -> Settings -> Webhooks -> Add New Webhook
#   URL     https://<your domain>/api/razorpay/webhook
#   Secret  anything long and random  (openssl rand -hex 32)
#   Events  payment.captured
#
# Paste the same string here. Unset, the callback refuses everything with a
# 503 rather than accepting unsigned deliveries — an endpoint that switches
# paid plans on must be a closed door when it is not configured, never an
# open one.
RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# ── The sandbox ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Switches a plan on with no payment, for development. It is ignored the
# moment the Razorpay pair above is set — the real provider always wins — but
# it must not exist in production all the same.
COSTBOOK_BILLING_SANDBOX=
